Third-party attributions and design influences
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Oncoskill's safety/scope/citation/abstain design was informed by, and adapts patterns
from, the following open-source work. Where ideas or structure were learned, original
text was written for Oncoskill; no third-party text is reproduced verbatim unless its
license clearly permits it (see research/source-ledger.yaml for the audit).

- AI-for-cancer-patients (Roupen92), Apache License 2.0.
  Safety/scope rules, citation/evidence-ledger pattern, reading-level and "abstain"
  design were adapted with attribution. Upstream ships no NOTICE file; the Apache-2.0
  license text and this attribution are retained, and modifications are stated.
  https://github.com/Roupen92/AI-for-cancer-patients

- OncoTeam (peter-fusek), MIT License.
  Care-ops task decomposition was used as a learn-from architectural reference.
  https://github.com/peter-fusek/oncoteam

- patiently-ai (PharmaTools.AI), inside FreedomIntelligence/OpenClaw-Medical-Skills.
  Used as a STRUCTURE reference ONLY for the document-explainer module. No text copied:
  the upstream repository has no LICENSE file (an MIT badge only) and the skill is
  third-party branded, so verbatim reuse is not assumed. See source-ledger.yaml.

Clinical reference facts are attributed to their primary sources (e.g. ESMO, ESGO/ESTRO,
NCI, HSE, Chordoma Foundation) inline and in research/source-ledger.yaml. Oncoskill is
not endorsed by any of these organizations.
